From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiaoge-tou <85100527+Tiaoge-tou@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:20:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Resolution, host side: measured render size in the state
 page, host-filled mode sizes, nn::oe default resolution

The host half of the resolution service (patch port 0075, group M of the port inventory), carried from the Tiaoge-tou/nxnative fork.

loader.c: dm_fps_state_apply writes the measured render size into the frame-step state page (the docked pair at +0x38 from DM_RENDER_WIDTH, the handheld pair at +0x40 from DM_RENDER_WIDTH_HD, with the narrow-screen stock-frame rules and the serve_narrow exception for a guest with a resolution record, published as DM_SERVE_NARROW for nn::oe), and fills a guest's display-mode size words from the screen (fixups HOST_FILL_D / HOST_FILL_H / HOST_FILL_W, parsed in read_layout, the fields in dm.h). The state page range check grows to +0x48 for the handheld cell.

hle_oe.c: the default display resolution answer follows the same sizes: the host's render width at the docked height for a display_wide profile with fullscreen on (the Hades II row lands with this patch), and the host's handheld size at 720p in handheld mode under the same narrow rule.

dm.h also declares dm_display_hz / dm_display_set_hz here: the definition and its callers land in the 120 Hz patch, and nothing calls them yet.

dm/tools/docs_patches.py classifies the four profile keys patch 0072 added (display_wide, pad_skin_toggle, serve_patch, display_hz) in SWITCH_BINDING: the generated game-patches doc refuses an unclassified key, and this patch is the first to have a profile use one.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Measured render sizes served to Silksong and Hades II on every size channel (PROJECT.md Phase 2)
Issue: Tiaoge-tou/NX2Apple PROJECT.md Phase 2

